    {
      "id": "p0121-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "A young comedian monster named Snowdrake gets his name from the English words \"snowflake\" and \"drake'', a type of dragon. Toby knew this wordplay might be tough to translate, so he left a note: \"you can call him a bird if it makes it easier to make a pun [ ... ] the main thing about him is that he's a comedian\".",
        "raw": "A young comedian monster named Snowdrake gets his name from the English\nwords \"snowflake\" and \"drake'', a type of dragon. Toby knew this wordplay\nmight be tough to translate, so he left a note: \"you can call him a bird if it makes\nit easier to make a pun [ ... ] the main thing about him is that he's a comedian\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09297457,
          0.23805714,
          0.70611519,
          0.30377143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09093498,
          0.23734286,
          0.70815478,
          0.30484286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "年轻的喜剧演员怪物 Snowdrake，名字来自英语 snowflake（雪花）与 drake（一种龙）。Toby 知道这个文字游戏可能难译，所以留了条说明：“如果把他叫作鸟能更方便地造双关，就这么办吧［……］最重要的是，他是个喜剧演员。”",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09486119,
          0.23662857,
