    {
      "id": "p0121-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Based on Toby’s suggestion, the translator renamed the monster owaraichō, a combination of owarai (\"comedy\") and chō (\"bird\"). This name is also a play on the word raichō (\"rock ptarmigan\"), a bird associated with cold, snowy areas.",
        "raw": "Based on Toby's suggestion, the translator renamed the monster owaraichO, a\ncombination of owarai (\"comedy\") and cha (\"bird\"). This name is also a play on\nthe word raich6 (\"rock ptarmigan\"), a bird associated with cold, snowy areas.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09486119,
          0.31897857,
          0.70333115,
          0.36980714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09093498,
